{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049044 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059748 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059557 :question/math-academy-id "e-4434" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if <div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-10 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059980 :question/math-academy-id "q-1079" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{det}(A)$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-6 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060000 :question/math-academy-id "q-11648" :question/problem "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{vmatrix}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244112 :question/math-academy-id "q-1080" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{det}(X)$, if\n    $X=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(X) & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40-(-3) \\\\  & =43\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253262 :question/math-academy-id "q-11646" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{det}(L)$, if\n    $L=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(L) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =12-(-10) \\\\  & =22\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262796 :question/math-academy-id "q-127578" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -9 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}| & =5\\cdot 7-(-9)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =35-27 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262797 :question/math-academy-id "q-127580" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =-1\\cdot 5-(-10)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-5-20 \\\\  & =-25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299591 :question/math-academy-id "q-317335" :question/problem "Calculate $det(R)$ given that\n$R=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(R)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(8)(4)-(-5)(3) \\\\  & =32+15 \\\\  & =47.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299592 :question/math-academy-id "q-317336" :question/problem "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2)(3)-(4)(1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299593 :question/math-academy-id "q-317342" :question/problem "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6)(7)-(-2)(5) \\\\  & =42+10 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510588 :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{det}(X)$, if\n$X=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & -11 \\\\ -13 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(X) & =|\\begin{aligned}-10 & -11 \\\\ -13 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-10\\cdot 7-(-11)\\cdot (-13) \\\\  & =-70-143 \\\\  & =-213\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510602 :question/problem "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -9 \\\\ -7 & -10\\end{vmatrix}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 \\\\ -7 & -10\\end{aligned}| & =-1\\cdot (-10)-(-9)\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =10-63 \\\\  & =-53\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510611 :question/problem "Calculate $det(R)$ given that\n$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 14 \\\\ -7 & 13\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(R)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 14 \\\\ -7 & 13\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-8)(13)-(14)(-7) \\\\  & =-104+98 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510612 :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -12 \\\\ 7 & -15\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & -12 \\\\ 7 & -15\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(7)(-15)-(-12)(7) \\\\  & =-105+84 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510613 :question/problem "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}-9 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-9)(9)-(1)(9) \\\\  & =-81-9 \\\\  & =-90.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510614 :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}-15 & -11 \\\\ 10 & -15\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-15 & -11 \\\\ 10 & -15\\end{aligned}| & =-15\\cdot (-15)-(-11)\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =225-(-110) \\\\  & =335\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510617 :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}-13 & 11 \\\\ 12 & -12\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-13 & 11 \\\\ 12 & -12\\end{aligned}| & =-13\\cdot (-12)-11\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =156-132 \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Integer Entries"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059749 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059558 :question/math-academy-id "e-4435" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if <div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059981 :question/math-academy-id "q-1088" :question/problem "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059982 :question/math-academy-id "q-1089" :question/problem "Calculate $det(Z)$, if\n $Z=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(Z) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-y\\cdot {y}^{2} \\\\  & =x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244117 :question/math-academy-id "q-1083" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}2x & {y}^{2} \\\\ z & -3\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2x & {y}^{2} \\\\ z & -3\\end{aligned}| & =2x\\cdot (-3)-{y}^{2}\\cdot z \\\\  & =-6x-{y}^{2}z\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244154 :question/math-academy-id "q-1087" :question/problem "Calculate $det(T)$, if\n    $T=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & 17 \\\\ 1 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 17 \\\\ 1 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 10-17\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5-17 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262800 :question/math-academy-id "q-127601" :question/problem "Calculate $det(C)$, if\n    $C=\\begin{bmatrix}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}-x & -2y \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & 5y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-x\\cdot 5y-(-2y)\\cdot \\frac{x}{2} \\\\  & =-5xy+xy \\\\  & =-4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262802 :question/math-academy-id "q-127603" :question/problem "Calculate $det(D)$, if\n    $D=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & y \\\\ -5 & xy\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2x\\cdot xy-y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}y+5y \\\\  & =y(2{x}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292870 :question/math-academy-id "q-275595" :question/problem "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & y \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & y \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-y\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299596 :question/math-academy-id "q-317367" :question/problem "Calculate $det(D)$ given that\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(D)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299597 :question/math-academy-id "q-317368" :question/problem "Calculate $det(E)$ given that\n$E=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(E)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-10 \\\\  & =-\\frac{37}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299598 :question/math-academy-id "q-317372" :question/problem "Calculate $det(D)$ given that\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n$det(D)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3x\\cdot x-2y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299599 :question/math-academy-id "q-317374" :question/problem "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}-y\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335990 :question/math-academy-id "q-69649" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{x} & {z}^{2} \\\\ 2y & -\\sqrt{x}\\end{aligned}| & =3\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x})-{z}^{2}\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-3x-2y{z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335991 :question/math-academy-id "q-69650" :question/problem "Calculate $det(H)$, if\n    $H=\\begin{bmatrix}-2r & 3s \\\\ -2t & 3u\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(H) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2r & 3s \\\\ -2t & 3u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2r\\cdot 3u-3s\\cdot (-2t) \\\\  & =-6ru-(-6st) \\\\  & =-6ru+6st \\\\  & =6(st-ru)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510569 :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{9}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{9} & -\\frac{9}{7}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{7})-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{9}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{45}{56}-(-\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{113}{280}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510573 :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{7} & -\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{7} & -\\frac{9}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{4}{5})-(-\\frac{9}{5})\\cdot \\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}-(-\\frac{9}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{55}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510575 :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{9} & -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{9} & -\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & -\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{9}\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{3})-(-\\frac{4}{7})\\cdot \\frac{2}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{27}-(-\\frac{8}{49}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1784}{1323}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510576 :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{5} & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{9}{5} & -\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{7}\\cdot (-\\frac{5}{4})-\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{9}{5}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{28}-(-\\frac{21}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{513}{140}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510583 :question/problem "Calculate $det(A)$ given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{7} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(A)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{7} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & \\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{35}-\\frac{5}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{113}{210}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix With Non-Integer Entries"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059750 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059559 :question/math-academy-id "e-4436" :question/problem "If\n${A} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        2 & -1  \\\\\n        -3 & k\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack$\nand\n$\\det({A}) = 5$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=5,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =5 \\\\ 2k-3 & =5 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060001 :question/math-academy-id "q-11651" :question/problem "If\n$C = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & k\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$det(C) = 3$, what is the value of $k$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060195 :question/math-academy-id "q-19801" :question/problem "If\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 + t & 2t \\\\ -3 & 1 - t\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(A) = 10$, what is the value of $t$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233379 :question/math-academy-id "q-127614" :question/problem "If\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}2x & 6 \\\\ 2x & x-2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(D)=-32$, what is the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2x & 6 \\\\ 2x & x-2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (x-2)-6\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-16x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-32$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x & =-32 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-16x+32 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+16 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253266 :question/math-academy-id "q-11653" :question/problem "If\n    $M=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(M)=2$, what is the value of $w?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & w \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-w\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4w.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nSince $det(M)=2$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =2 \\\\ 6-4w & =2 \\\\ -4w & =2-6 \\\\ -4w & =-4 \\\\ w & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262803 :question/math-academy-id "q-127604" :question/problem "If\n    $U=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(U)=-1$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 2k & -k+2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-k+2)-(-5)\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =7k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-1$, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-1 \\\\ 7k+6 & =-1 \\\\ 7k & =-1-6 \\\\ 7k & =-7 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262804 :question/math-academy-id "q-127606" :question/problem "If\n$T=\\begin{bmatrix}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(T)=-4$, what is the value of $v?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}v & 2v \\\\ 2 & v+8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot (v+8)-2v\\cdot 2 \\\\  & ={v}^{2}+4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(T)=-4$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v & =-4 \\\\ {v}^{2}+4v+4 & =0 \\\\ (v+2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ v & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262805 :question/math-academy-id "q-127607" :question/problem "If\n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(P)=-9$, what is the value of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =|\\begin{aligned}r-3 & r \\\\ 3 & r\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(r-3)\\cdot r-r\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={r}^{2}-6r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(P)=-9$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r & =-9 \\\\ {r}^{2}-6r+9 & =0 \\\\ (r-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ r & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262806 :question/math-academy-id "q-127608" :question/problem "If\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(B)=1$, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =|\\begin{aligned}5-p & p \\\\ 3 & p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5-p)\\cdot p-p\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-{p}^{2}+2p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(B)=1$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p & =1 \\\\ -{p}^{2}+2p-1 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-2p+1 & =0 \\\\ (p-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262807 :question/math-academy-id "q-127609" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(A)=-27$, what is the value of $y?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3y & y \\\\ 3 & y-5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3y\\cdot (y-5)-y\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-18y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=-27$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y & =-27 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-18y+27 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y+9 & =0 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292872 :question/math-academy-id "q-275598" :question/problem "If\n    $C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(C)=-14,$ determine the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(C) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-k\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(C)=-14$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C) & =-14 \\\\ 6-4k & =-14 \\\\ -4k & =-14-6 \\\\ -4k & =-20 \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292873 :question/math-academy-id "q-275601" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(A)=7,$ what is the value of $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+p & 4p-{p}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5-p\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+p)(5-p)-(4p-{p}^{2})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =15-3p+5p-{p}^{2}-4p+{p}^{2} \\\\  & =15-2p-\\cancel{{p}^{2}}+\\cancel{{p}^{2}} \\\\  & =15-2p.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $det(A)=7$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =7 \\\\ 15-2p & =7 \\\\ -2p & =-8 \\\\ p & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299600 :question/math-academy-id "q-317377" :question/problem "If\n    $D=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\text{det}(D)=-11,$ determine the value of $m.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-m\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10-3m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-11 \\\\ 10-3m & =-11 \\\\ -3m & =-21 \\\\ m & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299601 :question/math-academy-id "q-317382" :question/problem "If\n$U=\\begin{bmatrix}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(U)=-6$, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1+r)\\cdot 4-(2-r)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =4+4r+10-5r \\\\  & =14-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ 14-r & =-6 \\\\ -r & =-20 \\\\ r & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299602 :question/math-academy-id "q-317385" :question/problem "If\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(S)=25,$ what is the value of $s?$\n\n$s=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+s)(3-s)-2s(-4) \\\\  & =9-{s}^{2}+8s \\\\  & =-{s}^{2}+8s+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s+9 & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s-16 & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}-8s+16 & =0 \\\\ (s-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ s & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335992 :question/math-academy-id "q-69661" :question/problem "If\n$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $det(S)=2$, what is the value of $p?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1-p & 1+p \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1-p)\\cdot 2-(1+p)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2-2p+3+3p \\\\  & =5+p\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=2$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =2 \\\\ 5+p & =2 \\\\ p & =2-5 \\\\ p & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown in an Expression Involving the Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :topic/title "The Determinant of a 2x2 Matrix"}
